<title>UK: UK to rule on EMU when situation clear - govt source.</title>
<headline>UK to rule on EMU when situation clear - govt source.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain will not make up its mind on whether to join a single European currency until all ramifications of monetary union have been addressed, a senior government official said on Monday.  </p>
<p>The official was commenting on Chancellor fo the Exchequer Kenneth Clarke's comment, in a radio interview, on Sunday, that single currency only to decide later that it wanted to join.</p>
<p>&quot;The government has a settled position on a single currency. We are not going to take any decision until we've seen every ramification of a single currency thoroughly addressed,&quot; the official said.</p>
<p>He said Britain's right to opt out of monetary union put it in a perfect position, he said, adding that many questions about the single currency still had to be answered.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom 44-171-542 7717</p>
</text>
